{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1542","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E2. Abnormal Permutation Pairs (hard version)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is the hard version of the problem. The only difference between the easy version and the hard version is the constraints on $$$n$$$. You can only make hacks if both versions are solved."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A permutation of $$$1, 2, \\ldots, n$$$ is a sequence of $$$n$$$ integers, where each integer from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ appears exactly once. For example, $$$[2,3,1,4]$$$ is a permutation of $$$1, 2, 3, 4$$$, but $$$[1,4,2,2]$$$ isn't because $$$2$$$ appears twice in it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recall that the number of inversions in a permutation $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ is the number of pairs of indices $$$(i, j)$$$ such that $$$i \\lt j$$$ and $$$a_i \\gt a_j$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ be two permutations of $$$1, 2, \\ldots, n$$$. Find the number of permutation pairs $$$(p,q)$$$ that satisfy the following conditions:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p$$$ is lexicographically smaller than $$$q$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the number of inversions in $$$p$$$ is greater than the number of inversions in $$$q$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the number of such pairs modulo $$$mod$$$. Note that $$$mod$$$ may not be a prime."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$mod$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 500$$$, $$$1\\le mod\\le 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer, which is the answer modulo $$$mod$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 403458273\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n17"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following are all valid pairs $$$(p,q)$$$ when $$$n=4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[1,3,4,2]$$$, $$$q=[2,1,3,4]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[1,4,2,3]$$$, $$$q=[2,1,3,4]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[1,4,3,2]$$$, $$$q=[2,1,3,4]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[1,4,3,2]$$$, $$$q=[2,1,4,3]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[1,4,3,2]$$$, $$$q=[2,3,1,4]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[1,4,3,2]$$$, $$$q=[3,1,2,4]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[2,3,4,1]$$$, $$$q=[3,1,2,4]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[2,4,1,3]$$$, $$$q=[3,1,2,4]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[2,4,3,1]$$$, $$$q=[3,1,2,4]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[2,4,3,1]$$$, $$$q=[3,1,4,2]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[2,4,3,1]$$$, $$$q=[3,2,1,4]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[2,4,3,1]$$$, $$$q=[4,1,2,3]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[3,2,4,1]$$$, $$$q=[4,1,2,3]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[3,4,1,2]$$$, $$$q=[4,1,2,3]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[3,4,2,1]$$$, $$$q=[4,1,2,3]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[3,4,2,1]$$$, $$$q=[4,1,3,2]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p=[3,4,2,1]$$$, $$$q=[4,2,1,3]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E2","problemCode":"1542E2","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1542/problem/E2"}